---
import BaseLayout from '../components/BaseLayout.astro';
import Circle from '../components/Circle.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="ACCESSIBILITY" description="Accessibility commitments and known limitations for Original.">
  <header class="page-head">
    <h1 class="page-title"><Circle /> ACCESSIBILITY</h1>
    <p class="lede">The target, what is implemented, and how to report a barrier. Last updated 2026-11-04.</p>
  </header>

  <div class="prose legal-prose">
    <p>
      Original is a text-first site. The target is WCAG 2.2 Level AA for the public pages, with
      the understanding that a small static site cannot guarantee conformance for every browser,
      assistive technology, or external link.
    </p>

    <h2>WHAT IS IMPLEMENTED</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Semantic headings, landmarks, lists, tables, and form labels.</li>
      <li>A visible skip link and a visible keyboard focus indicator.</li>
      <li>Text and controls that remain usable at 200% zoom and on narrow screens.</li>
      <li>No autoplaying media, no decorative animation, and no color-only status labels.</li>
      <li>Red on white with contrast chosen for body text and controls.</li>
      <li>ARIA labels on icon-only or stateful controls where the text alone is not enough.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>KNOWN LIMITATIONS</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The site has not been tested with every screen reader and browser combination.</li>
      <li>Some third-party links and embedded external pages are outside this site's control.</li>
      <li>The full-screen CLI is a specialist interface; its static text endpoints are the accessible alternative.</li>
      <li>Very long checksums and source URLs may wrap awkwardly at narrow widths.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>REPORT A BARRIER</h2>
    <p>
      If a page or tool is difficult to use, write to
      <a href="mailto:contact@original.wales">contact@original.wales</a> with the URL, the assistive
      technology you use, and what happened. Reports are used to fix the site, not published
      without permission.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
